  "summary": "Tools now link GWAS loci to genes and cell contexts via fine-mapped eQTLs, colocalization, single-cell chromatin data and variant-function graphs.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is moving from GWAS association signals to candidate effector genes and relevant cell contexts. CAS-X combines fine-mapped eQTL PIPs and allelic fold changes across five metabolic tissues to prioritize genes at type 2 diabetes loci. CELL-X extends this to islet single-cell atlases for beta-cell-relevant prioritization. EPIC2 ranks trait-relevant cell types by linking GWAS summary statistics to single-cell chromatin accessibility while modeling linkage disequilibrium. CellColocDB provides coloc.abf colocalization across bulk, sorted-cell and single-cell data, and the IGVF Catalog integrates 657 variant-function datasets into a knowledge graph. A second strand refines association and prediction. SIQReg optimizes phenotype scale to improve GWAS, TWAS and polygenic prediction in UK Biobank. A regularized ensemble builds PRS from summary statistics alone, and GiMat tests gene-gene interactions across multiple dichotomous phenotypes. Fine-tuned Borzoi and AlphaGenome match, but do not exceed, variant-based linear models for expression prediction in an admixed population.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
